@startuml
title D6 — Surefyre Integration Architecture
caption How Surefyre exchanges transaction, document, rating and identity data

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 210
skinparam maxMessageSize 120
skinparam nodesep 75
skinparam ranksep 85
skinparam padding 18

skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderThickness 1.4
}

rectangle "Surefyre\n\nAgent Portal\nUnderwriting Workbench\nRules and Workflow" as Surefyre #EAF4EA

rectangle "Integration Configuration\n\n• Endpoint URLs\n• Authentication\n• Field mappings\n• Request / response rules\n• Error handling" as Integration #FFF4CC

rectangle "AIM\n\nCore insurance operations\nand policy transactions" as AIM #FFF1DF

rectangle "ImageRight\n\nDocuments, correspondence\nand workflow references" as ImageRight #EAF2FF

rectangle "Carrier / Rating Services\n\nRates, quote results,\npolicy or bind responses" as Carrier #F1ECFA

rectangle "Third-Party Data Services\n\nAddress validation,\nrisk enrichment,\nreference data" as ThirdParty #F3F8E8

rectangle "Identity and Access\n\nOAuth, API tokens,\nBasic Auth, SSO" as Identity #E8F7F5

Surefyre -right-> Integration : Business event\nor user action

Integration -right-> AIM : JSON / XML\nREST or SOAP
AIM -left-> Integration : Transaction ID,\nstatus or error

Integration -right-> ImageRight : Document metadata,\nindex values or request
ImageRight -left-> Integration : Document ID,\nlink or workflow status

Integration -right-> Carrier : Rating, quote,\nbind or policy request
Carrier -left-> Integration : Rate, decision,\nconfirmation or error

Integration -right-> ThirdParty : Data inquiry
ThirdParty -left-> Integration : Enriched or\nvalidated data

Surefyre -down-> Identity : Login or service\nauthentication request
Identity -up-> Surefyre : Token, session\nor access result

Integration -left-> Surefyre : Normalized response,\nstatus or error message

legend bottom
|= Integration concern |= Technical Consultant focus |
| Endpoint | Correct environment-specific URL and service path |
| Authentication | OAuth, tokens, Basic Auth, SSO or customer-specific security |
| Mapping | Surefyre fields mapped to JSON, XML or target-system fields |
| Validation | Required headers, parameters, payload structure and data types |
| Testing | Postman requests, positive and negative cases, response verification |
| Error handling | Reproduce failure, inspect response, log evidence and coordinate resolution |
| Documentation | Record configuration, mappings, dependencies and deployed changes |
endlegend

note bottom of Integration
Interview model only.
Actual protocols, system-of-record ownership and integration direction
must be confirmed with SPG for each customer and program.
end note

@enduml
